Subject: the session reads Raye's own application menu, decided in the code

Raye ships nine application categories -- raye-applications.menu and nine
.directory files -- and a three-line session environment script that
exported XDG_MENU_PREFIX=raye- so that KSycoca would read them. The
categories were installed, correct, and never read, on every account, since
the day they were written.

🚨 Measured on 2026-11-06 against this source:

    startplasma-wayland.cpp:66   runEnvironmentScripts();
    startplasma-wayland.cpp:72   setupPlasmaEnvironment();
    startplasma.cpp:410            qputenv("XDG_MENU_PREFIX", "plasma-");

and the same order in startplasma-x11.cpp, at 58 and 62. The environment
scripts are sourced BEFORE the session's environment is set up, and the line
above overwrites the variable unconditionally. So the script did its job and
six lines of control flow later the value was gone.

⚠️ And no other mechanism outside the source could have done it either,
which is what makes this a patch rather than a configuration change:

  * a profile snippet, PAM's environment or the login manager all set the
    variable before startplasma even runs, so the same line overwrites them;
  * systemd's own environment is not a way round it: syncDBusEnvironment()
    sends this process's environment to the activation environment AFTER
    setupPlasmaEnvironment() has run, and importSystemdEnvrionment(), which
    runs after that, skips every name beginning with XDG_ (isSessionVariable).
    So the value that reaches every program of the session is this one.

This is the third time this tree has paid for the same shape -- a Raye
setting written somewhere nothing reads -- after the layout reached through
KPackage's fallback (0001 of this component) and the containment binding
written under a containment id instead of a type (plasma-desktop/0002). It is
also the same shape of test failure: theme/shell/menus/tests sets
XDG_MENU_PREFIX=raye- itself before running, so the categories were checked
against the prefix Raye wanted and never against the prefix the session has.

The prefix is now chosen where it is set, in a header of two inline
functions, and the Raye test that comes with it checks the two properties
that matter: that the value names the file Raye installs, dash included, and
that it REPLACES an inherited value rather than filling in a missing one. The
second is the whole point -- a helper that only wrote when the variable was
empty would hand the desktop whichever outside mechanism spoke last, which is
the bug with a different cause.

⚠️ What this patch does NOT claim. It makes the menu reachable; it does not
measure what changes on screen. The Raye Start applet asks Kicker's RootModel
with flat: true and showAllAppsCategorized: false, so its All apps list is
A-Z either way and only moves where the two menu files differ in which
applications they include at all. What plainly changes is every view that
shows categories -- the menu editor and the application pickers -- and which
Include/Exclude rules decide where an application lands. Measuring the
difference between the two menus needs a session, and belongs there.

Reason: this cannot be done outside the source. XDG_MENU_PREFIX is set
unconditionally inside setupPlasmaEnvironment(), after every out-of-source
mechanism has already run, and the session's environment is published from
this process afterwards -- so there is no file, script, look-and-feel package
or systemd unit that can decide which application menu a Plasma session
reads. The three-line environment script this replaces is the proof: it is
installed, it runs, and it does nothing.

--- a/startkde/startplasma.cpp
